.SH "Highlights"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Fast\&. Probably the fastest\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Supports multiple and negative patterns\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Synchronous, Promise and Stream API\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Object mode\&. Can return more than just strings\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Error-tolerant\&.
.PP
.SH "Old and modern mode"
.PP
This package works in two modes, depending on the environment in which it is used\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBOld mode\fP\&. Node\&.js below 10\&.10 or when the \fB`stats`\fP option is \fIenabled\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBModern mode\fP\&. Node\&.js 10\&.10+ and the \fB`stats`\fP option is \fIdisabled\fP\&.
.PP

.PP
The modern mode is faster\&. Learn more about the \fRinternal mechanism\fP\&.
.SH "Pattern syntax"
.PP
.RS 4
:warning: Always use forward-slashes in glob expressions (patterns and \fB`ignore`\fP option)\&. Use backslashes for escaping characters\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
There is more than one form of syntax: basic and advanced\&. Below is a brief overview of the supported features\&. Also pay attention to our \fBFAQ\fP\&.

.PP
.RS 4
:book: This package uses \fR\fRmicromatch\fP\fP as a library for pattern matching\&. 
.RE
.PP
.SS "Basic syntax"
.IP "\(bu" 2
An asterisk (\fR*\fP) — matches everything except slashes (path separators), hidden files (names starting with \fR\&.\fP)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
A double star or globstar (\fR**\fP) — matches zero or more directories\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Question mark (\fR?\fP) – matches any single character except slashes (path separators)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Sequence (\fR[seq]\fP) — matches any character in sequence\&.
.PP

.PP
.RS 4
:book: A few additional words about the \fRbasic matching behavior\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Some examples:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRsrc/**/*\&.js\fP — matches all files in the \fRsrc\fP directory (any level of nesting) that have the \fR\&.js\fP extension\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRsrc/*\&.??\fP — matches all files in the \fRsrc\fP directory (only first level of nesting) that have a two-character extension\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRfile-[01]\&.js\fP — matches files: \fRfile-0\&.js\fP, \fRfile-1\&.js\fP\&.
.PP
.SS "Advanced syntax"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fREscapes characters\fP (\fR\\\\\fP) — matching special characters (\fR$^*+?()[]\fP) as literals\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRPOSIX character classes\fP (\fR[[:digit:]]\fP)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRExtended globs\fP (\fR?(pattern-list)\fP)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRBash style brace expansions\fP (\fR{}\fP)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRRegexp character classes\fP (\fR[1-5]\fP)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRRegex groups\fP (\fR(a|b)\fP)\&.
.PP

.PP
.RS 4
:book: A few additional words about the \fRadvanced matching behavior\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Some examples:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRsrc/**/*\&.{css,scss}\fP — matches all files in the \fRsrc\fP directory (any level of nesting) that have the \fR\&.css\fP or \fR\&.scss\fP extension\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRfile-[[:digit:]]\&.js\fP — matches files: \fRfile-0\&.js\fP, \fRfile-1\&.js\fP, …, \fRfile-9\&.js\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRfile-{1\&.\&.3}\&.js\fP — matches files: \fRfile-1\&.js\fP, \fRfile-2\&.js\fP, \fRfile-3\&.js\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRfile-(1|2)\fP — matches files: \fRfile-1\&.js\fP, \fRfile-2\&.js\fP\&.
.PP
.SH "Installation"
.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install fast\-glob
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "Asynchronous"
.PP
.nf
fg(patterns, [options])
fg\&.async(patterns, [options])
fg\&.glob(patterns, [options])
.fi
.PP

.PP
Returns a \fRPromise\fP with an array of matching entries\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const fg = require('fast\-glob');

const entries = await fg(['\&.editorconfig', '**/index\&.js'], { dot: true });

// ['\&.editorconfig', 'services/index\&.js']
.fi
.PP
.SS "Synchronous"
.PP
.nf
fg\&.sync(patterns, [options])
fg\&.globSync(patterns, [options])
.fi
.PP

.PP
Returns an array of matching entries\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const fg = require('fast\-glob');

const entries = fg\&.sync(['\&.editorconfig', '**/index\&.js'], { dot: true });

// ['\&.editorconfig', 'services/index\&.js']
.fi
.PP
.SS "Stream"
.PP
.nf
fg\&.stream(patterns, [options])
fg\&.globStream(patterns, [options])
.fi
.PP

.PP
Returns a \fR\fRReadableStream\fP\fP when the \fRdata\fP event will be emitted with matching entry\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const fg = require('fast\-glob');

const stream = fg\&.stream(['\&.editorconfig', '**/index\&.js'], { dot: true });

for await (const entry of stream) {
    // \&.editorconfig
    // services/index\&.js
}
.fi
.PP
